<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN GUY SPITAELS RESIGNS FROM PARLIAMENT, CCB.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN GUY SPITAELS RESIGNS FROM PARLIAMENT, CCB.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Guy Spitaels, former Parti Socialiste (PS) chairman, has resigned from the Walloon parliament and from his function as chairman of the Credit Communal/Gemeentekrediet , a PS official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official, confirming a report on Belgian news agency Belga, said she was not sure whether Spitaels was staying on as mayor of the city of Ath.  </p>
<p>Belgian radio said this morning that Spitaels had told the Belgian judiciary that he knew about illegal funds obtained by his party in the late eighties.</p>
<p>The PS has been at the centre of a bribery scandal involving French firm Dassault.</p>
<p>Dassault denies all wrong doing.</p>
